RV_LOAD("FS",{"lang": "EN", "stale": {"files": [], "anchors": []}, "hub": "形式语言是「问题」的抽象: 先定义字母表和字符串, 再把语言看成字符串的集合并做运算.", "branches": [{"id": "comp", "zh": "语言与计算", "de": "Languages & Computation", "one": "自然语言和形式语言的区别, 以及计算为什么归结为判定成员关系.", "a0": -2.0719, "a1": -1.0697}, {"id": "str", "zh": "字母表与字符串", "de": "Alphabets & Strings", "one": "字母表是有限的符号集合, 字符串是符号的有限序列.", "a0": -0.9697, "a1": -0.3971}, {"id": "sops", "zh": "字符串的运算", "de": "String Operations", "one": "连接、长度、下标、出现次数、反转和幂.", "a0": -0.2971, "a1": 0.5618}, {"id": "lops", "zh": "语言及其运算", "de": "Languages and Operations", "one": "语言是全语言的子集, 所以集合运算和连接都能用在语言上.", "a0": 0.6618, "a1": 1.5208}, {"id": "fsa", "zh": "有限状态自动机", "de": "Finite State Automata", "one": "只看当前状态和当前输入的机器: 输入带、读头、控制单元, 读完后看停在哪个状态.", "a0": 1.6208, "a1": 2.7661}, {"id": "fdef", "zh": "形式定义", "de": "Formal Definition", "one": "把自动机写成五元组, 转移函数可以列出来、画成图或写成转移表.", "a0": 2.8661, "a1": 3.5819}, {"id": "cmpl", "zh": "完全与不完全的 FSA", "de": "Complete & Incomplete FSA", "one": "每个状态对每个符号都有转移的是完全的; 缺转移就停机拒绝, 补一个陷阱状态就变完全.", "a0": 3.6819, "a1": 4.1113}], "nodes": [{"id": "natfor", "b": "comp", "zh": "自然语言与形式语言", "de": "Natural & Formal Languages", "one": "都把内容赋给符号表达式; 自然语言自发演变, 形式语言为特定用途人为创造.", "pts": ["共同点: 都受规则支配, 都有句法和语义", "结构成分: 字母表 + 文法", "形式语言精确、无歧义, 自然语言灵活、常有歧义"], "ex": "", "ang": -1.6862, "lv": 0, "rr": 0.125, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "sprache", "dd": "A language is a system that assigns content to symbolic expressions; natural languages evolve through social interaction, formal languages are artificially created for a specific purpose.", "xp": "自然语言 (natural language) 是人和动物交流用的, 多模态 (声音、文字、手势), 在社会交往中自发演变, 灵活但常有歧义. 形式语言 (formal language) 为编程、逻辑、数学等用途人为设计, 精确、无歧义, 规则必须严格遵守, 只通过受控的修订流程改变 (如 Python 的 PEP). 两者的共同点是: 都受规则支配, 都有句法 (syntax) 和语义 (semantics), 都由字母表 (alphabet) 和文法 (grammar) 构成.", "sub": [{"id": "natfor.sharedrules", "zh": "共同点", "de": "", "one": "都受规则支配, 都有句法和语义, 都用于交流."}, {"id": "natfor.struct", "zh": "结构成分", "de": "Alphabet & Grammar", "one": "字母表提供符号, 文法提供产生式规则."}, {"id": "natfor.synsem", "zh": "句法与语义", "de": "Syntax & Semantics", "one": "句法管怎样构造句子, 语义管表达什么意义."}], "tm": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], "q": "Used by humans (and animals) to communicate between each other", "fol": "Slide 2"}, {"id": "flsw", "b": "comp", "zh": "形式语言的优点和缺点", "de": "Strengths and Weaknesses of Formal Languages", "one": "精确、可预测、互操作、省资源; 但不灵活、只在特定领域有效.", "pts": ["优点: 确定性 (同样输入同样输出)", "缺点: 每多一种情况都要改规则", "不擅长歧义和不确定性, 正好和大语言模型互补"], "ex": "SQL: SELECT name FROM students WHERE semester = 1", "ang": -1.2742, "lv": 1, "rr": 0.375, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "staerken", "dd": "Formal languages offer precision, interoperability and resource efficiency, but are inflexible and domain-specific.", "xp": "优点: 精确、可预测, 结果是确定的 (determinism); 互操作性 (interoperability) 让同一个 HTML 文件在各种设备上都能显示; 对定义明确的简单问题计算量小; 适合处理结构化数据 (SQL). 缺点: 不灵活, 每多一种情况都要手工改规则; 领域专用 (domain specificity), 多半只在逻辑、封闭类这类特定领域有效; 擅长逻辑推理, 不擅长歧义、创造性和不确定性. 这些缺点正是大语言模型的长处.", "sub": [{"id": "flsw.precise", "zh": "精确与确定", "de": "Precision & Determinism", "one": "同样的输入总得到同样的输出."}, {"id": "flsw.interop", "zh": "互操作性", "de": "Interoperability", "one": "在不同系统和设备上都能用."}, {"id": "flsw.resource", "zh": "节省资源", "de": "Resource Efficiency", "one": "简单问题计算量小、速度快."}, {"id": "flsw.inflex", "zh": "不灵活", "de": "", "one": "适应变化要不断手工更新规则."}, {"id": "flsw.domain", "zh": "领域专用", "de": "Domain Specificity", "one": "效果好但多半只在特定领域."}], "tm": [5, 6, 7], "q": "Interoperability → work on different systems and devices (e.g., HTML)", "fol": "Slide 5"}, {"id": "member", "b": "comp", "zh": "成员关系与转换", "de": "Membership & Transduction", "one": "问题可以写成语言 (判断串在不在集合里) 或语言之间的转换 (输入串 → 输出串).", "pts": ["分类任务: 整数 n 是偶数吗", "变换任务: \"3+5\" → \"8\""], "ex": "\"3+5\" → \"8\"", "ang": -1.8674, "lv": 1, "rr": 0.625, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "warum", "dd": "Problems can be described as languages, i.e. sets of strings (classification), or as transductions between languages (transformation).", "xp": "形式语言可以看成「问题」这个概念的抽象. 分类任务: 把所有偶数的十进制写法看成一个语言, 问字符串 n 在不在里面. 变换任务 (transduction): 把输入串 \"3+5\" 转换成输出串 \"8\". 偶数这个问题只看最后一位, 一个正则表达式就能判断, 这预告了后面的自动机.", "sub": [{"id": "member.clftask", "zh": "分类任务", "de": "Classification Task", "one": "判断给定的串在不在集合里."}, {"id": "member.transtask", "zh": "变换任务", "de": "Transformation Task", "one": "把输入串转换成输出串."}], "tm": [8, 9], "q": "Determining the membership in a set of strings", "fol": "Slide 8"}, {"id": "compu", "b": "comp", "zh": "计算", "de": "Computation", "one": "所有计算都归结为判定成员关系或在串集合之间映射, 两者可以互相代替.", "pts": ["等价不等于一样快", "计算需要基本元素和组合规则", "可重复性: 同样的输入总得到同样的输出"], "ex": "", "ang": -1.4666, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.625, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "berechnung", "dd": "All computational processes can be reduced to determining membership in a set of strings or mapping between sets of strings; the two tasks are interchangeable.", "xp": "不直接计算 3 + 5, 也可以定义语言 L = {所有正确的等式}, 依次问 \"3+5=0\" 在不在 L 里、\"3+5=1\" 在不在……直到找到 8. 两种做法等价, 但速度可能差很多; 反过来有些问题验证答案容易、直接求解难 (数独). 计算是对信息的自动处理, 需要基本元素 (primitives) 和组合规则, 计算机建在 0/1 和逻辑运算上. 可重复性 (replicability) 要求同样的输入总得到同样的输出. 这和形式语言同构: 字母表 = 基本元素, 文法 = 组合规则, 语言 = 能组合出的所有串.", "sub": [{"id": "compu.interchange", "zh": "两种任务可互换", "de": "", "one": "映射可以改成逐个测试候选答案的成员关系."}, {"id": "compu.prim", "zh": "基本元素", "de": "Primitives", "one": "计算用规则把基本元素组合成复杂结构."}, {"id": "compu.repli", "zh": "可重复性", "de": "Replicability", "one": "同样的输入必须总得到同样的输出."}], "tm": [10, 11], "q": "Computers are built on those basic primitives (0/1) and operations over them (and/or/not/xor/. . . )", "fol": "Slide 9"}, {"id": "turing", "b": "comp", "zh": "图灵机", "de": "Turing Machine", "one": "图灵首次把算法和计算形式化; 图灵机是通用计算机的理论模型.", "pts": ["无限长纸带、读写头、有限个状态和转移规则", "图灵测试: 评判者能否分辨人和机器"], "ex": "", "ang": -1.2742, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.875, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "turing", "dd": "Alan Turing provided the first formalisation of algorithm and computation; the Turing machine is a theoretical model of a general purpose computer.", "xp": "图灵机 (1936) 由一条无限长的纸带、一个读写头、有限个状态和转移规则组成. 有限自动机只能往前读, 图灵机还能在纸带上来回读写, 是这门课最后讲到的最强计算模型. 图灵测试 (Turing test, 1950) 问机器是否真有智能: 人类评判者用自然语言同时和人、机器对话, 看能否分辨出机器.", "sub": [{"id": "turing.tm", "zh": "图灵机", "de": "Turing Machine", "one": "纸带、读写头、有限状态和转移规则."}, {"id": "turing.ttest", "zh": "图灵测试", "de": "Turing Test", "one": "评判者能否在对话中分辨人和机器."}], "tm": [12, 13], "q": "The Turing machine: a theoretical model of a general purpose computer", "fol": "Slide 10"}, {"id": "clhist", "b": "comp", "zh": "计算语言学的发展", "de": "The Evolution of Computational Linguistics", "one": "从规则系统到统计模型、深度学习, 再到大语言模型.", "pts": ["1954 Georgetown 实验: 机器翻译的开端", "1956 乔姆斯基谱系: 这门课的主线", "1990 年代转向数据驱动"], "ex": "", "ang": -1.675, "lv": 0, "rr": 0.375, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "geschichte", "dd": "Computational linguistics evolved from early machine translation and rule-based systems to statistical models, deep learning and large language models.", "xp": "1950 年代: Georgetown 实验 (1954) 自动翻译 60 多个俄语句子, 是机器翻译的开端. 1960 年代: 基于规则的系统, 乔姆斯基谱系 (Chomsky hierarchy, 1956) 按文法能力把形式语言分成四级, 是这门课的主线; ELIZA 用模式匹配和改写规则模仿对话. 1990 年代转向统计模型和大型标注语料库, 2010 年代深度学习 (BERT), 2020 年代大语言模型. 讲者用 ChatGPT 画的时间线拼写全错, 说明大模型在精确的符号和结构上会出错.", "sub": [{"id": "clhist.rule", "zh": "基于规则的系统", "de": "Rule-Based Systems", "one": "1960 年代: 乔姆斯基谱系、形式文法、ELIZA."}, {"id": "clhist.chomsky", "zh": "乔姆斯基谱系", "de": "Chomsky Hierarchy", "one": "按文法能力把形式语言分成四级."}, {"id": "clhist.datadriven", "zh": "数据驱动", "de": "Data-Driven Approaches", "one": "1990 年代起转向统计模型和标注语料."}], "tm": [14]}, {"id": "hybrid", "b": "comp", "zh": "形式语言与大语言模型", "de": "Formal Languages and Large Language Models", "one": "混合系统结合两者: LLM 提供知识和处理歧义, 形式语言提供精确和结构化推理.", "pts": ["今天形式语言用于形态 (自动机)、句法 (上下文无关文法)、语义", "例: LLM 把问题翻成 SQL 再精确执行"], "ex": "", "ang": -1.675, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.875, "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "heute", "dd": "Today formal languages are used for very specific tasks in CL, and hybrid systems combine them with large language models.", "xp": "今天形式语言在计算语言学里用于具体任务: 音系和形态用自动机理论 (如有限状态转换器把词形映射到 Lemma), 句法用上下文无关文法 (context-free grammar), 形式语义用谓词逻辑表示. 混合系统在一个系统里结合两种架构: LLM 提供世界知识、创造力和处理歧义的能力, 形式语言提供精确和结构化推理. 例如让 LLM 把问题翻成 SQL 再由数据库执行, 或用文法约束 LLM 输出合法的 JSON.", "sub": [{"id": "hybrid.apps", "zh": "今天的应用", "de": "", "one": "形态用自动机, 句法用上下文无关文法."}, {"id": "hybrid.hybridsys", "zh": "混合系统", "de": "Hybrid Systems", "one": "LLM 管知识和歧义, 形式语言管精确推理."}], "tm": [15], "q": "syntactic structures → Context-free grammars", "fol": "Slide 14"}, {"id": "alpha", "b": "str", "zh": "字母表", "de": "Alphabet", "one": "有限且非空的符号集合, 记作 Σ.", "pts": ["空集不算字母表", "无穷多个符号也不算", "符号也可以是整个词"], "ex": "Σ = {0, 1}", "ang": -0.7494, "lv": 1, "rr": 0.167, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "def-alphabet", "dd": "An alphabet is a finite and non-empty set of symbols.", "xp": "字母表 (alphabet) 习惯记作 Σ, 必须同时满足有限和非空: 空集不算, 无穷多个符号也不算. 「符号」只是不可再分的单位, 不一定是字母: Σ = {0, 1} 只有两个符号; 计算语言学里也常把整个词当成一个符号, 这样字符串就是词序列, 也就是句子.", "sub": [{"id": "alpha.finite", "zh": "有限且非空", "de": "Finite and Non-Empty", "one": "空集和无穷集合都不是字母表."}, {"id": "alpha.symbol", "zh": "符号", "de": "Symbol", "one": "不可再分的单位, 可以是字母、数字或整个词."}], "tm": [16], "q": "An alphabet is a finite and non-empty set of symbols", "fol": "Slide 2"}, {"id": "string", "b": "str", "zh": "字符串", "de": "String", "one": "字母表中符号组成的有序且有限的序列, 也叫词; 空串 ε 不含任何符号.", "pts": ["有序: ab 和 ba 不同", "有限: 每个串都有确定长度", "ε 不是符号, 是长度为 0 的串"], "ex": "", "ang": -0.6175, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.5, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "def-string", "dd": "A string (or word) is any ordered and finite sequence of symbols from an alphabet; the empty string ε is the sequence with no symbols.", "xp": "字符串 (string) 是语言的基本元素. 「有序」意味着 ab 和 ba 是两个不同的串; 「有限」意味着每个串都有确定的长度. 只要每个位置上的符号都来自字母表就合法, 和有没有意义无关. 空串 (empty string) ε 不是符号, 而是长度为 0 的串, 所以 ε ∉ Σ; 还要分清空集 ∅ (一个串都没有) 和 {ε} (只含空串). 课本 Linz 用 λ 表示空串.", "sub": [{"id": "string.ordered", "zh": "有序且有限", "de": "Ordered and Finite", "one": "ab 和 ba 不同, 每个串都有确定长度."}, {"id": "string.eps", "zh": "空串", "de": "Empty String", "one": "不含任何符号的串, 记作 ε."}], "tm": [17, 18], "q": "Strings are the basic elements of a language", "fol": "Slide 3"}, {"id": "univ", "b": "str", "zh": "全语言", "de": "Universal Language", "one": "字母表上所有串的集合 Σ*, 总是包含空串.", "pts": ["按长度再按字典序可以一个不漏地数下去", "长度为 n 的串有 |Σ|ⁿ 个"], "ex": "Σ* = {ε, a, b, aa, ab, …}", "ang": -0.8529, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.833, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "universal", "dd": "The universal language Σ* is the set of all strings over a given alphabet; it always contains the empty string.", "xp": "Σ* 读作 Sigma star, 星号叫 Kleene 星号. 列举时先按长度, 同长度再按字典序 (shortlex 顺序): 长度 0 的 1 个, 长度 1 的 |Σ| 个, 长度 n 的 |Σ|ⁿ 个. 所以 Σ* 是无穷集合, 但每个元素都是有限串, 并且可以一个不漏地数下去.", "sub": [{"id": "univ.kleene", "zh": "Kleene 星号", "de": "Kleene Star", "one": "零次或多次."}, {"id": "univ.shortlex", "zh": "列举顺序", "de": "Shortlex Order", "one": "先按长度, 同长度再按字典序."}], "tm": [19, 21], "q": "Universal language: The set of all strings over a given alphabet", "fol": "Slide 5"}, {"id": "plus", "b": "str", "zh": "正闭包", "de": "Positive Closure", "one": "字母表上除空串以外所有串的集合 Σ⁺.", "pts": ["Σ⁺ = Σ* ∖ {ε}", "星号 = 零次或多次, 加号 = 一次或多次"], "ex": "Σ⁺ = Σ* ∖ {ε}", "ang": -0.6239, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.833, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "plus", "dd": "The positive closure Σ⁺ is the set of all strings over an alphabet except the empty string.", "xp": "两者的关系: Σ⁺ = Σ* ∖ {ε}, 反过来 Σ* = Σ⁺ ∪ {ε}. 星号表示零次或多次, 加号表示一次或多次, 这和后面正则表达式里的 * 与 + 是同一个意思.", "sub": [{"id": "plus.starplus", "zh": "星号与加号", "de": "", "one": "星号允许零次, 加号至少一次."}], "tm": [20]}, {"id": "konkat", "b": "sops", "zh": "连接", "de": "Concatenation", "one": "把第二个串的符号接在第一个串后面, 写作 wv.", "pts": ["满足结合律, 不满足交换律", "空串是单位元: wε = εw = w"], "ex": "aab · cb = aabcb", "ang": 0.3064, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "konkat", "dd": "The concatenation of two strings w and v is the string wv obtained by appending the symbols of v after those of w.", "xp": "连接 (concatenation) 写作 w · v, 点通常省略. aab 接上 cb 得到 aabcb. 连接满足结合律, 但不满足交换律 (一般 wv ≠ vw). 空串是单位元: wε = εw = w, 作用就像乘法里的 1, 所以后面幂的零次方定义成 ε.", "sub": [{"id": "konkat.assoc", "zh": "结合律", "de": "Associativity", "one": "(wv)u = w(vu)."}, {"id": "konkat.unit", "zh": "单位元", "de": "Neutral Element", "one": "空串不改变任何串."}], "tm": [22], "q": "Powers of a L: concatenation for a certain number of times", "fol": "Slide 18"}, {"id": "len", "b": "sops", "zh": "长度", "de": "Length", "one": "串中符号的个数, 记作 |w|; 空串长度为 0.", "pts": ["连接时长度相加", "竖线用在集合上表示元素个数"], "ex": "|wv| = |w| + |v|", "ang": -0.0417, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "laenge", "dd": "The length |w| of a string is the number of symbols in it.", "xp": "aab 的长度是 3, 空串长度为 0. 连接时长度相加: |wv| = |w| + |v|. 同样的竖线用在集合上表示元素个数, 要看竖线里是串还是集合来区分.", "sub": [{"id": "len.addlen", "zh": "长度相加", "de": "", "one": "|wv| = |w| + |v|."}], "tm": [23], "q": "Static (cannot be modified) and with finite length", "fol": "Slide 6"}, {"id": "index", "b": "sops", "zh": "下标", "de": "Index", "one": "wᵢ 是从左数第 i 个位置上的符号, 合法范围 1 ≤ i ≤ |w|.", "pts": ["从 1 开始数, Python 从 0 开始", "空串没有合法下标"], "ex": "", "ang": 0.1873, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "index", "dd": "The index wᵢ of a string is the symbol at the i-th position from the left, with 1 ≤ i ≤ |w|.", "xp": "下标 (index) 从 1 开始数, Python 从 0 开始: 幻灯片的 w₁ 对应 Python 的 w[0]. 合法范围由长度决定, 所以空串没有任何合法下标.", "sub": [{"id": "index.fromone", "zh": "从 1 开始", "de": "", "one": "和 Python 的 0 起始不同."}], "tm": [24]}, {"id": "occ", "b": "sops", "zh": "符号出现次数", "de": "Symbol Occurrence Number", "one": "|w|ₜ 是符号 t 在 w 中出现的次数.", "pts": ["所有符号的出现次数之和等于长度", "用来定义语言, 如 a 和 b 一样多的串"], "ex": "Σ |w|ₜ = |w|", "ang": -0.1517, "lv": 0, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "vorkommen", "dd": "The symbol occurrence number |w|ₜ indicates how many times the symbol t occurs in the string w.", "xp": "对应 Python 的 w.count('a'). 字母表里有但串里没出现的符号, 次数是 0. 把每个符号的出现次数加起来就是串的长度. 后面定义语言时常用它, 例如「a 和 b 一样多的串」写作 {w : |w|ₐ = |w|_b}.", "sub": [{"id": "occ.sumlen", "zh": "次数之和", "de": "", "one": "所有符号的出现次数加起来等于长度."}], "tm": [25]}, {"id": "rev", "b": "sops", "zh": "反转", "de": "Reverse", "one": "把串的符号倒过来写, 记作 wᴿ.", "pts": ["反转两次回到原串", "连接后反转要对调顺序", "wᴿ = w 的串叫回文"], "ex": "(wv)ᴿ = vᴿwᴿ", "ang": 0.0774, "lv": 0, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "reverse", "dd": "The reverse wᴿ of a string is obtained by writing its symbols in reverse order.", "xp": "aab 反转是 baa. 反转两次回到原串: (wᴿ)ᴿ = w. 连接后再反转, 两个串的顺序要对调: (wv)ᴿ = vᴿwᴿ. 反转后和自己相同的串叫回文 (palindrome), 例如 aba.", "sub": [{"id": "rev.revconc", "zh": "连接的反转", "de": "", "one": "(wv)ᴿ = vᴿwᴿ."}, {"id": "rev.palin", "zh": "回文", "de": "Palindrome", "one": "wᴿ = w 的串."}], "tm": [26, 27]}, {"id": "pow", "b": "sops", "zh": "幂", "de": "Exponentiation", "one": "wⁿ 是把 w 和自己连接 n 次, 约定 w⁰ = ε.", "pts": ["|wⁿ| = n · |w|", "同一个串重复, 不能换串"], "ex": "(aab)³ = aabaabaab", "ang": 0.4164, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "power", "dd": "The exponentiation wⁿ of a string is obtained by concatenating the string with itself n times, with w⁰ = ε.", "xp": "(aab)³ = aabaabaab, 对应 Python 的 'aab' * 3. 约定 w⁰ = ε, 所以 |wⁿ| = n · |w|. 串的幂是同一个串重复; 后面语言的幂 Lⁿ 每次可以从 L 里各选一个串, 两者不一样.", "sub": [{"id": "pow.zero", "zh": "零次幂", "de": "", "one": "w⁰ = ε."}], "tm": [28]}, {"id": "lang", "b": "lops", "zh": "语言", "de": "Language", "one": "全语言 Σ* 的任意子集; 语言里的串叫句子.", "pts": ["句子个数有限是有限语言, 否则是无限语言", "空集和 {ε} 都是语言, 但不同"], "ex": "{aⁿbⁿ : n ≥ 1}", "ang": 0.8073, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "sprache", "dd": "A language L is any subset of the universal language Σ*; a string in a language is called a sentence.", "xp": "语言 (language) 的定义非常宽: 字母表上任意一个串集合都是语言. 句子个数有限的叫有限语言 (finite language), 否则是无限语言 (infinite language). {aⁿbⁿ : n ≥ 1} (先 n 个 a 再同样多个 b) 是课上的重要例子: 有限自动机认不出它, 要用上下文无关文法. 空集 ∅ 和 {ε} 都是语言, 但不同.", "sub": [{"id": "lang.sent", "zh": "句子", "de": "Sentence", "one": "语言里的一个串."}, {"id": "lang.fininf", "zh": "有限语言与无限语言", "de": "Finite vs. Infinite Language", "one": "看句子个数是否有限."}, {"id": "lang.anbn", "zh": "aⁿbⁿ", "de": "", "one": "先 n 个 a 再 n 个 b, 有限自动机认不出."}], "tm": [29, 30, 31, 32], "q": "If the language has a finite number of sentences, this is a finite language", "fol": "Slide 15"}, {"id": "setops", "b": "lops", "zh": "并与交", "de": "Union & Intersection", "one": "并 = 至少属于一个语言的串, 交 = 同时属于两个语言的串.", "pts": ["结果仍是同一字母表上的语言"], "ex": "L₁ = {a, ab}, L₂ = {ab, b}: L₁ ∩ L₂ = {ab}", "ang": 1.0363, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "union", "dd": "The union of two languages is the set of strings valid in at least one of them; the intersection is the set of strings valid in both.", "xp": "语言是集合, 集合运算可以直接用. 并 (union) 的「或」包括两者都属于的情况; 交 (intersection) 要求同时属于两个语言. 例: L₁ = {a, ab}, L₂ = {ab, b}, 则 L₁ ∪ L₂ = {a, ab, b}, L₁ ∩ L₂ = {ab}. 结果仍是同一字母表上的语言.", "sub": [{"id": "setops.union", "zh": "并", "de": "Union", "one": "至少属于一个语言."}, {"id": "setops.inter", "zh": "交", "de": "Intersection", "one": "同时属于两个语言."}], "tm": [33, 34], "q": "Union: the set of strings valid in at least one of the languages", "fol": "Slide 16"}, {"id": "compl", "b": "lops", "zh": "补与差", "de": "Complement & Difference", "one": "补 = Σ* 中不属于 L 的串; 差 = 属于 L₁ 但不属于 L₂ 的串.", "pts": ["补总是相对 Σ* 取", "有限语言的补一定是无限语言", "差 = L₁ 和 L₂ 的补取交"], "ex": "L₁ − L₂ = L₁ ∩ L̄₂", "ang": 1.2654, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "komplement", "dd": "The complement of L contains all strings of Σ* not in L; the difference L₁ − L₂ contains the strings in L₁ but not in L₂.", "xp": "补 (complement) 总是相对全语言 Σ* 取, 所以有限语言的补一定是无限语言. 差 (difference) 等于 L₁ 和 L₂ 的补取交: L₁ − L₂ = L₁ ∩ L̄₂.", "sub": [{"id": "compl.relsigma", "zh": "相对全语言", "de": "", "one": "补永远在 Σ* 里取."}, {"id": "compl.diffint", "zh": "差等于交补", "de": "", "one": "L₁ − L₂ = L₁ ∩ L̄₂."}], "tm": [35, 36]}, {"id": "lconc", "b": "lops", "zh": "语言的连接", "de": "Concatenation of Languages", "one": "从 L₁ 取一个串、从 L₂ 取一个串拼起来, 所有这样的串组成 L₁L₂.", "pts": ["不满足交换律", "L{ε} = L", "L∅ = ∅"], "ex": "", "ang": 0.9172, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "komplement", "dd": "The concatenation of two languages L₁L₂ is the set of all strings wv with w from L₁ and v from L₂.", "xp": "语言的连接是笛卡尔积式的: 从 L₁ 取一个串、从 L₂ 取一个串拼起来, 所有组合都算. 和串的连接一样不满足交换律. 两个特殊情况: L{ε} = L (空串不改变任何串), L∅ = ∅ (没有串可以和它配对).", "sub": [{"id": "lconc.lepsilon", "zh": "与 {ε} 连接", "de": "", "one": "L{ε} = L."}, {"id": "lconc.lempty", "zh": "与空集连接", "de": "", "one": "L∅ = ∅."}]}, {"id": "lpow", "b": "lops", "zh": "语言的幂与反转", "de": "Power & Reverse", "one": "Lⁿ 递归定义为 L⁰ = {ε}, Lⁿ⁺¹ = LⁿL; 语言的反转是把每个串分别反转.", "pts": ["每次连接都可以从 L 里重新选串", "L⁰ = {ε} 而不是 ∅"], "ex": "{a, b}² = {aa, ab, ba, bb}", "ang": 1.1463, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "potenz", "dd": "The power of a language is defined recursively as L⁰ = {ε} and Lⁿ⁺¹ = LⁿL; the reverse of a language reverses each of its strings.", "xp": "语言的幂 (power) 每次连接都可以从 L 里重新选串, 所以 {a, b}² = {aa, ab, ba, bb}, {a, b}³ 是全部 8 个长度为 3 的串. L⁰ = {ε} 而不是 ∅: {ε} 是语言连接的单位元, 这样 L¹ = L⁰L = L 才成立; 若取 ∅, 所有的幂都会变成空集. 语言的反转是把每个串分别反转, 不是把集合元素的顺序倒过来.", "sub": [{"id": "lpow.lzero", "zh": "L⁰ = {ε}", "de": "", "one": "单位元, 不能取空集."}, {"id": "lpow.lrev", "zh": "语言的反转", "de": "Reverse of a Language", "one": "每个串分别反转."}], "tm": [37], "q": "Powers of a L: concatenation for a certain number of times", "fol": "Slide 18"}, {"id": "prio", "b": "lops", "zh": "运算的优先级", "de": "Priority of Operations", "one": "先算一元运算 (幂、星号、加号、反转), 再算连接, 最后算集合运算.", "pts": ["想先做并就必须加括号", "后面读正则表达式时同样按这个顺序"], "ex": "L₁ ∪ L₂L₃* = L₁ ∪ (L₂ · (L₃*))", "ang": 1.3753, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "prioritaet", "dd": "Without brackets, unary operations are applied first, then concatenation, then set operations.", "xp": "优先级和算术「先乘方、再乘、最后加」同构: 一元运算 (幂、星号、加号、反转) 最先, 连接其次, 并、交、差最后. L₁ ∪ L₂L₃* 要读成 L₁ ∪ (L₂ · (L₃*)); 想先做并就必须加括号: (L₁ ∪ L₂)L₃*. 后面写正则表达式时同样按这个顺序读.", "sub": [{"id": "prio.order", "zh": "运算顺序", "de": "Order of Operations", "one": "一元运算 → 连接 → 集合运算."}, {"id": "prio.brackets", "zh": "括号", "de": "", "one": "改变默认顺序必须加括号."}]}, {"id": "nomem", "b": "fsa", "zh": "没有记忆的系统", "de": "Systems with no Memory", "one": "输出或下一个状态只由当前状态和当前输入决定, 不需要记住以前的输入.", "pts": ["过去输入里有用的信息体现在当前状态上", "闸机、售货机、红绿灯、字符串搜索", "状态有限, 能记住的东西也有限"], "ex": "", "ang": 1.8544, "lv": 0, "rr": 0.125, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "ohne-speicher", "dd": "Systems where the output or the next state is determined solely by the current state and the current input, without any need to remember past inputs.", "xp": "这类系统不另外保存输入的历史, 过去输入里有用的那一点信息已经体现在当前状态上 (current state). 售货机不记得先投了 1 分还是 2 分, 只记得「已经投了 3 分」. 闸机、售货机、红绿灯、数字电路和字符串搜索都是这样, 都可以实现成有限状态自动机 (finite state automaton). 状态个数有限, 能记住的信息也有限, 这就是有限自动机的能力边界.", "sub": [{"id": "nomem.nomemex", "zh": "例子", "de": "", "one": "闸机、自动售货机、红绿灯、数字电路、字符串搜索."}, {"id": "nomem.curstate", "zh": "当前状态", "de": "", "one": "过去输入里有用的信息全在当前状态里."}]}, {"id": "fsm", "b": "fsa", "zh": "有限状态自动机", "de": "Finite State Automaton", "one": "画成有向图: 节点是状态, 有向边是转移, 边上的标签是触发转移的输入.", "pts": ["状态: 系统停留一段时间的情形", "转移: 瞬间发生的动作", "是最简单的自动机"], "ex": "开关: ON 经 switch off 到 OFF", "ang": 2.0743, "lv": 1, "rr": 0.375, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "graph", "dd": "A finite state automaton is represented as a directed graph: a finite set of nodes (states) connected by a set of directed arcs (transitions).", "xp": "有限状态自动机画成有向图 (directed graph): 圆圈是状态 (state), 是系统停留一段时间的情形; 带标签的箭头是转移 (transition), 是瞬间发生的动作, 标签是触发它的输入. 例如电灯开关只有 ON 和 OFF 两个状态, switch off 从 ON 到 OFF, switch on 回到 ON. 它由输入带、读头和控制单元三部分组成, 是最简单的自动机.", "sub": [{"id": "fsm.fsmstate", "zh": "状态", "de": "State", "one": "系统停留一段时间的情形."}, {"id": "fsm.fsmtrans", "zh": "转移", "de": "Transition", "one": "瞬间发生的动作, 箭头上标着触发它的输入."}, {"id": "fsm.fsmextra", "zh": "更复杂的模型", "de": "", "one": "加额外记忆、输出或左右移动的读头, 能力更强."}], "tm": [38, 39, 40], "q": "Can all be implemented as finite state automata", "fol": "Slide 3"}, {"id": "tape", "b": "fsa", "zh": "输入带", "de": "Input Tape", "one": "存放要处理的输入串, 只含字母表里的符号, 静态、长度有限、从左到右读.", "pts": ["不能改写, 中间结果写不回带上", "图灵机的带可以写"], "ex": "", "ang": 2.5324, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.375, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "dd": "The input tape contains the input string to be processed; it contains only symbols from the alphabet, is static, has finite length and is read from left to right.", "xp": "输入带 (input tape) 上只有字母表 Σ 里的符号, 长度有限, 而且是静态的: 不能改写. 自动机没法把中间结果写回带上, 所以它唯一的记忆是控制单元里的当前状态. 以后的图灵机可以写带, 读头还能左右移动, 能力强得多.", "sub": [{"id": "tape.tapesym", "zh": "只含字母表符号", "de": "", "one": "带上的每个符号都来自 Σ."}, {"id": "tape.tapestatic", "zh": "静态", "de": "", "one": "不能修改, 长度有限."}], "tm": [42], "q": "Contains the input string to be processed", "fol": "Slide 6"}, {"id": "head", "b": "fsa", "zh": "读头", "de": "Reader Head", "one": "从最左边的符号开始, 一次读一个符号再右移一格, 不能后退也不能改带.", "pts": ["长度为 n 的串正好走 n 步", "每个符号只看一次"], "ex": "", "ang": 2.0743, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.875, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "dd": "The reader head reads one symbol at a time, starting with the leftmost symbol, and then moves one step to the right; it cannot move backward or modify the tape.", "xp": "读头 (reader head) 从最左边的符号开始, 读一个符号就右移一格, 不能后退也不能改写. 所以长度为 n 的串, 自动机正好走 n 步就结束, 每个符号只看一次, 这也是有限自动机识别字符串很快的原因.", "sub": [{"id": "head.headleft", "zh": "从最左边开始", "de": "", "one": "初始化时读头放在最左边的符号上."}, {"id": "head.headright", "zh": "一步右移", "de": "", "one": "每读一个符号右移一格, 不能后退."}], "tm": [43], "q": "Reads a symbol and then moves one step to the right", "fol": "Slide 7"}, {"id": "cunit", "b": "fsa", "zh": "控制单元", "de": "Control Unit", "one": "决定状态之间的转移, 由记住当前状态的状态寄存器和转移函数 δ 组成.", "pts": ["唯一的记忆就是当前状态"], "ex": "", "ang": 1.8544, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.625, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "dd": "The control unit determines transitions between states; it consists of the state register, which tracks the current state, and the transition function δ.", "xp": "控制单元 (control unit) 有两部分: 状态寄存器 (state register) 记住当前状态, 转移函数 δ (transition function) 给出「在这个状态读到这个符号, 下一步去哪里」. 有限自动机的有限记忆就在这里, 只用来记状态.", "sub": [{"id": "cunit.register", "zh": "状态寄存器", "de": "State Register", "one": "记住当前状态."}, {"id": "cunit.cudelta", "zh": "转移函数", "de": "Transition Function", "one": "由当前状态和输入符号算出下一个状态."}], "tm": [44, 45], "q": "Determines transitions between states", "fol": "Slide 8"}, {"id": "workflow", "b": "fsa", "zh": "三部分如何协同工作", "de": "How They Work Together", "one": "初始化到初始状态, 逐个符号经 δ 换状态, 读完时在终态就接受, 否则拒绝.", "pts": ["只看读完整个串后的状态", "中途经过终态不算"], "ex": "baa!: 1 → 2 → 3 → 3 → 4, 接受", "ang": 2.5324, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.875, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "ablauf", "dd": "Initialization sets the control unit to the start state; each symbol is read and the next state computed via δ; at the end of the input the FSA accepts if it is in an accept state and rejects otherwise.", "xp": "运行分三步. 初始化: 输入串放上带, 读头在最左边, 控制单元置于初始状态 q₀ (start state). 处理: 读当前符号, 用当前状态和这个符号经 δ 算出下一个状态, 读头右移, 重复. 结束: 读完输入就停机, 在接受状态 (accept state, final state) 就接受 (accept), 否则拒绝 (reject). 只看读完整个串之后的状态, 中途经过终态不算.", "sub": [{"id": "workflow.init", "zh": "初始化", "de": "Initialization", "one": "读头在最左边, 控制单元在 q₀."}, {"id": "workflow.proc", "zh": "处理", "de": "Processing", "one": "读符号、经 δ 换状态、右移, 重复."}, {"id": "workflow.term", "zh": "结束", "de": "Termination", "one": "读完输入后在终态就接受, 否则拒绝."}]}, {"id": "dfa", "b": "fsa", "zh": "确定性有限自动机", "de": "Deterministic FSA", "one": "每个状态和每个输入符号恰好有一个转移, 行为完全可预测.", "pts": ["确定只管同一状态同一符号不能有两个去向", "严格定义下 δ 是全函数"], "ex": "", "ang": 2.3125, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.625, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "det", "dd": "In a deterministic FSA, for every state and input symbol there is exactly one transition to a new state; its behaviour is completely predictable.", "xp": "确定性有限自动机 (deterministic FSA, DFA) 的行为只由当前状态和输入决定, 完全可预测. 「确定」只管同一状态、同一符号不能有两个去向; 某个符号有没有转移是完全与否的问题. 严格按 δ : Q × Σ → Q 的定义, δ 是全函数, DFA 一定是完全的; 课件也把缺转移的自动机叫 DFA, 那是把 δ 放宽成部分函数.", "sub": [{"id": "dfa.onetrans", "zh": "恰好一个转移", "de": "", "one": "每个状态和输入符号恰好对应一个下一状态."}, {"id": "dfa.predict", "zh": "完全可预测", "de": "", "one": "行为由当前状态和输入唯一决定."}], "tm": [48], "q": "For every state and input symbol, there is exactly one transition to a new state", "fol": "Slide 11"}, {"id": "nfa", "b": "fsa", "zh": "非确定性有限自动机", "de": "Nondeterministic FSA", "one": "同一状态、同一符号可以有多个转移, 机器可以在几条路径中选择.", "pts": ["光看当前状态和输入预测不了行为", "下一讲展开"], "ex": "", "ang": 2.3125, "lv": 0, "rr": 0.125, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "det", "dd": "A nondeterministic FSA may have multiple possible transitions for a given state and input symbol and can choose among multiple paths.", "xp": "非确定性有限自动机 (nondeterministic FSA, NFA) 在同一状态读同一符号时可以有几个去向, 机器可以在几条路径里「选择」, 所以光看当前状态和输入预测不了它的行为. 课件在这一讲只提了一下 (stay tuned), 下一讲展开.", "sub": [{"id": "nfa.multitrans", "zh": "多个可能的转移", "de": "", "one": "同一状态和符号可以有多个下一状态."}], "tm": [49], "q": "It may have multiple possible transitions for a given state and input symbol", "fol": "Slide 11"}, {"id": "quint", "b": "fdef", "zh": "五元组", "de": "Quintuple", "one": "有限状态自动机是五元组 (Σ, Q, q₀, δ, F): 字母表、状态集合、初始状态、转移函数、终态集合.", "pts": ["初始状态 q₀ ∈ Q", "终态 F ⊆ Q, 可以有多个", "各书五项顺序不同, 内容一样"], "ex": "M = ({a, b}, {q₁, q₂}, q₁, δ, {q₂})", "ang": 3.0121, "lv": 2, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "quintupel", "dd": "An FSA is a quintuple (Σ, Q, q₀, δ, F): input alphabet, set of states, initial state, transition function and final states.", "xp": "五元组 (quintuple) 把自动机的五个组成部分写全: 输入字母表 Σ, 有限的状态集合 Q, 初始状态 q₀ ∈ Q, 转移函数 δ : Q × Σ → Q, 终态集合 F ⊆ Q (可以有多个, 也可以为空). 读图时无起点的箭头 (或三角形) 指向初始状态, 双圈是终态. 课件写 (Σ, Q, q₀, δ, F), 练习和很多教材写 (Q, Σ, δ, q₀, F), 内容一样.", "sub": [{"id": "quint.qsigma", "zh": "输入字母表", "de": "Input Alphabet", "one": "自动机能读的符号."}, {"id": "quint.qstates", "zh": "状态集合", "de": "Set of States", "one": "有限个状态."}, {"id": "quint.qinit", "zh": "初始状态", "de": "Initial State", "one": "q₀ ∈ Q, 运行从这里开始."}, {"id": "quint.qfinal", "zh": "终态", "de": "Final States", "one": "F ⊆ Q, 读完时在这里就接受."}], "tm": [46, 50], "q": "Control unit set to the start state", "fol": "Slide 9"}, {"id": "delta", "b": "fdef", "zh": "转移函数", "de": "Transition Function", "one": "δ : Q × Σ → Q 规定自动机的状态怎样随输入符号变化, 决定一个串是否被接受.", "pts": ["逐条列出 δ(q, a) = p", "图上的箭头", "转移表"], "ex": "δ(q₁, b) = q₂", "ang": 3.2984, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.25, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "delta", "dd": "The transition function δ : Q × Σ → Q defines how the state of the automaton changes in response to an input symbol and determines whether a string is accepted.", "xp": "转移函数 (transition function) 把「状态, 符号」这一对映射到下一个状态. 它有三种等价写法: 逐条列出 δ(q₁, b) = q₂, 画成图上的箭头, 或写成转移表 (transition table). 一个串被不被接受, 由 δ 和终态集合一起决定. 课件 Slide 14 第一种写法把 δ(q₂, b) = q₂ 误印成了 δ(q₂, a) = q₂.", "sub": [{"id": "delta.dlist", "zh": "逐条列出", "de": "", "one": "δ(q₁, a) = q₁, δ(q₁, b) = q₂, …"}, {"id": "delta.dgraph", "zh": "状态图", "de": "", "one": "每条转移是一支带标签的箭头."}], "tm": [51], "q": "It defines how the state of the automaton changes in response to an input symbol", "fol": "Slide 14"}, {"id": "ttable", "b": "fdef", "zh": "转移表", "de": "Transition Table", "one": "行是状态, 列是输入符号, 格子里是下一个状态.", "pts": ["DFA 的表每格恰好一个状态", "有空格就是不完全的"], "ex": "", "ang": 3.0789, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "delta", "dd": "A transition table has the states as rows and the input symbols as columns; each cell gives the next state.", "xp": "转移表 (transition table) 把 δ 排成表: 第 q 行、a 列的格子就是 δ(q, a). DFA 的表每个格子恰好一个状态; 有空格说明缺转移, 是不完全的自动机. 练习里经常要在形式定义、转移表和图之间互相转换.", "tm": [52]}, {"id": "vend", "b": "fdef", "zh": "自动售货机", "de": "Vending Machine", "one": "状态记已投金额 0–5, 收 1、2、5 分, 总额到 5 就停在终态 5.", "pts": ["不记投币顺序, 只记金额", "多投的钱被吞掉 (不找零)"], "ex": "221: 0 → 2 → 4 → 5", "ang": 3.2698, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "automat", "dd": "A greedy vending machine with price 5 cents accepts any sequence of 1, 2 or 5 cent coins with total value 5 cents or bigger and returns no change.", "xp": "状态名就是已投金额 0–5, 从状态 s 投 c 分到 min(s + c, 5), 5 是终态并对三种硬币自环, 多投的钱被吞掉. 字母表是 {1, 2, 5}, 被接受的投币序列就是自动机接受的串: 11111、221、1112、5、11115; 11、21 钱不够, 被拒绝. 售货机不记投币顺序, 只记金额, 正是「没有记忆的系统」.", "sub": [{"id": "vend.vexact", "zh": "恰好够", "de": "", "one": "11111、221、1112、5."}, {"id": "vend.vmore", "zh": "投多了", "de": "", "one": "11115 也接受, 不找零."}, {"id": "vend.vless", "zh": "不够", "de": "", "one": "11、21 停在 2、3, 拒绝."}], "q": "Vending machines: get food if you insert money", "fol": "Slide 3"}, {"id": "sheep", "b": "fdef", "zh": "羊叫自动机", "de": "Sheep Talk", "one": "识别 b 后接一个以上的 a 再接 ! 的串, 四个状态、四个转移.", "pts": ["2 → 3 的 a 保证至少一个 a, 3 的自环允许更多", "是不完全的 DFA"], "ex": "ba!, baa! 接受; b!, baa 拒绝", "ang": 3.4607, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.75, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "uebung", "dd": "An FSA recognising sheep talk: strings that start with b, then one or more a, and end with !.", "xp": "状态 1 读 b 到 2, 2 读 a 到 3, 3 读 a 自环, 3 读 ! 到终态 4. 2 → 3 的 a 保证至少一个 a, 3 上的自环允许更多. 它只列了 4 个转移 (4 个状态 × 3 个符号本应有 12 个), 是不完全的 DFA; 加一个陷阱状态就能补成完全的. J&M 原书的羊叫是 baa+!, 课件简化成至少一个 a.", "sub": [{"id": "sheep.sheepok", "zh": "接受", "de": "", "one": "ba!、baa!、baaaa!."}, {"id": "sheep.sheepno", "zh": "拒绝", "de": "", "one": "b!、baa、aa!."}]}, {"id": "complete", "b": "cmpl", "zh": "完全的 FSA", "de": "Complete FSA", "one": "每个状态对字母表里每个符号都定义了转移, 任何输入串都能读到底.", "pts": ["转移表没有空格", "适合健壮的系统", "常带陷阱状态"], "ex": "识别含 aba 的串", "ang": 3.7821, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.5, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "complete", "dd": "A complete FSA has transitions defined for all input symbols in every state, contains no undefined transitions and always processes any input string.", "xp": "完全的 FSA (complete FSA) 的转移表没有空格, 任何输入串都能读到底. 适合需要健壮的系统, 显式处理所有可能的输入, 常常带一个陷阱状态. 例子: 识别含 aba 的串的 DFA, 状态记的是已经匹配到 aba 的前几个字母; 一旦出现 aba 就停在终态自环里.", "sub": [{"id": "complete.cmprobust", "zh": "健壮", "de": "", "one": "显式处理所有可能的输入."}, {"id": "complete.cmpaba", "zh": "含 aba 的串", "de": "", "one": "q₀ … q₃ 记已匹配到 aba 的前几个字母."}], "tm": [53], "q": "It has transitions defined for all input symbols", "fol": "Slide 18"}, {"id": "sink", "b": "cmpl", "zh": "陷阱状态", "de": "Sink State", "one": "一种非接受状态, 一旦进入就对每个符号都留在原地.", "pts": ["也叫 dead state、trap state", "收纳所有注定失败的输入"], "ex": "以 ab 开头的 DFA 里的 q₁", "ang": 3.8966, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.5, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "sink", "dd": "A sink state (dead state, trap state) is a non-accepting state that the FSA never leaves once entered.", "xp": "陷阱状态 (sink state) 对每个符号都自环, 而且不是终态. 完全的 FSA 要求每个状态对每个符号都有去向, 那些一出现就注定失败的输入就统一指向它. 例子: 识别以 ab 开头的串的 DFA 里, 开头读 b 或 aa 都进陷阱 q₁. 终态上的自环不叫陷阱状态.", "sub": [{"id": "sink.sinknames", "zh": "别名", "de": "", "one": "dead state、trap state."}, {"id": "sink.sinkuse", "zh": "用处", "de": "", "one": "处理不想要的输入、错误处理、简化设计."}], "tm": [55], "q": "Once entered, the FSA remains in this state", "fol": "Slide 20"}, {"id": "incompl", "b": "cmpl", "zh": "不完全的 FSA", "de": "Incomplete FSA", "one": "有些状态对某些输入缺转移; 遇到未定义的转移就停机拒绝.", "pts": ["状态和转移更少, 画起来简单", "加一个陷阱状态就能补成完全的", "识别能力和完全的相同"], "ex": "", "ang": 4.0111, "lv": 3, "rr": 0.5, "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "unvollst", "dd": "An incomplete FSA has missing transitions for certain inputs in some states; undefined transitions cause it to halt and reject the input.", "xp": "不完全的 FSA (incomplete FSA) 状态和转移更少, 画起来简单, 但未定义的情况可能要外部错误处理. 遇到缺的转移就直接停机拒绝, 不管后面还剩多少输入. 识别以 ab 开头的串, 去掉陷阱状态就得到不完全版; 反过来, 加一个陷阱状态、把缺的转移都指向它, 就补成完全的. 两者识别能力相同.", "sub": [{"id": "incompl.halt", "zh": "停机拒绝", "de": "", "one": "遇到未定义的转移就停, 拒绝输入."}, {"id": "incompl.tocomplete", "zh": "补成完全的", "de": "", "one": "加陷阱状态, 缺的转移都指向它."}], "tm": [54], "q": "This automaton has missing transitions for certain inputs in some states", "fol": "Slide 22"}], "edges": [["natfor", "flsw", ">", "形式语言精确、无歧义的特点决定了它的优点和缺点.", "FS-01-导论.html", "staerken"], ["natfor", "member", ">", "形式语言被用来把「问题」形式化.", "FS-01-导论.html", "warum"], ["natfor", "lang", ">", "课上把语言形式化为字符串的集合.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "sprache"], ["natfor", "alpha", ">", "两类语言的结构成分都是字母表和文法.", "FS-01-导论.html", "sprache"], ["member", "compu", ">", "所有计算都归结为判定成员关系或在串之间映射.", "FS-01-导论.html", "berechnung"], ["member", "lang", "~", "判定成员关系就是问一个串在不在某个语言里.", "FS-01-导论.html", "warum"], ["compu", "turing", ">", "图灵机是这种计算的理论模型.", "FS-01-导论.html", "turing"], ["compu", "alpha", "~", "计算的基本元素对应字母表, 组合规则对应文法.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "def-alphabet"], ["flsw", "hybrid", ">", "形式语言的缺点正由大语言模型补上.", "FS-01-导论.html", "staerken"], ["clhist", "hybrid", "~", "发展从规则走到统计和 LLM, 今天两条路开始结合.", "FS-01-导论.html", "geschichte"], ["alpha", "string", ">", "字符串是字母表上符号的有限序列.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "def-string"], ["string", "univ", ">", "全语言是所有字符串的集合.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "universal"], ["univ", "plus", ">", "正闭包是全语言去掉空串.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "alphabet"], ["string", "konkat", ">", "连接是对字符串的运算.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "konkat"], ["string", "len", ">", "长度是字符串的基本属性.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "laenge"], ["len", "index", ">", "合法下标的范围由长度决定.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "stringops"], ["occ", "len", "~", "所有符号的出现次数加起来就是长度.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "vorkommen"], ["konkat", "len", "~", "连接时长度相加.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "laenge"], ["konkat", "pow", ">", "幂是把同一个串重复连接.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "power"], ["konkat", "rev", "~", "连接后再反转, 两个串的顺序要对调.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "reverse"], ["univ", "lang", ">", "语言是全语言的子集.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "sprache"], ["lang", "setops", ">", "语言是集合, 并和交可以直接用.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "union"], ["lang", "compl", ">", "补和差也是集合运算.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "komplement"], ["univ", "compl", ">", "补总是相对全语言取.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "sprachen"], ["konkat", "lconc", ">", "语言的连接由串的连接定义.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "komplement"], ["lconc", "lpow", ">", "语言的幂是把语言和自己反复连接.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "sprachen"], ["pow", "lpow", "~", "串的幂重复同一个串, 语言的幂每次可以换一个串.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "power"], ["rev", "lpow", ">", "语言的反转是把每个串分别反转.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "potenz"], ["setops", "prio", ">", "集合运算的优先级最低.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "sprachen"], ["lconc", "prio", ">", "连接排在一元运算和集合运算之间.", "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "sprachen"], ["nomem", "fsm", ">", "没有记忆的系统都可以实现成有限状态自动机.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "ohne-speicher"], ["fsm", "tape", ">", "有限状态自动机由输入带、读头和控制单元组成.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "teile"], ["tape", "head", ">", "读头在输入带上从左到右读.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "teile"], ["fsm", "cunit", ">", "控制单元是自动机的第三个组成部分.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "teile"], ["head", "workflow", ">", "运行时读头每读一个符号就右移一格.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "ablauf"], ["cunit", "workflow", ">", "控制单元用当前状态和输入符号算出下一个状态.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "ablauf"], ["fsm", "dfa", ">", "有限自动机分确定的和非确定的两种.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "det"], ["dfa", "nfa", "~", "同一状态同一符号: 恰好一个转移还是可以有多个."], ["alpha", "quint", ">", "五元组的第一项就是输入字母表.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "quintupel"], ["fsm", "quint", ">", "五元组是有限状态自动机的形式定义.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "quintupel"], ["quint", "delta", ">", "转移函数是五元组的一项.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "delta"], ["cunit", "delta", "~", "控制单元靠转移函数 δ 决定下一个状态.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "delta"], ["delta", "ttable", ">", "转移表是转移函数的另一种写法.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "delta"], ["dfa", "ttable", ">", "DFA 的转移表每格恰好一个状态."], ["workflow", "vend", ">", "售货机读完硬币序列后停在终态 5 才接受.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "fsa"], ["workflow", "sheep", ">", "羊叫自动机按同样的步骤逐个读符号.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "ablauf"], ["lang", "workflow", "~", "自动机接受的串组成它识别的语言.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "sink"], ["delta", "complete", ">", "完全看的是转移函数对每对状态和符号是否都有定义."], ["complete", "sink", ">", "完全的 FSA 常用陷阱状态收纳注定失败的输入.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "sink"], ["complete", "incompl", "~", "有没有缺的转移.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "unvollst"], ["sink", "incompl", ">", "去掉陷阱状态和通向它的转移就得到不完全的 FSA.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "unvollst"], ["incompl", "sheep", "~", "课件的羊叫自动机是不完全的.", "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "uebung"], ["vend", "complete", "~", "售货机每个状态对 1、2、5 都有转移, 是完全的."]], "terms": [{"t": "natural language", "zh": "自然语言", "b": "comp", "d": "A language used by humans to communicate, developed spontaneously through social interaction.", "zd": "人类用来交流、在社会交往中自发形成的语言.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "Used by humans (and animals) to communicate between each other", "fol": "Slide 2", "vs": "formal language", "n": "natfor"}, {"t": "formal language", "zh": "形式语言", "b": "comp", "d": "A language deliberately created for a specific purpose such as programming, logic or mathematics.", "zd": "为编程、逻辑、数学等特定用途人为创造的语言.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "Used to formalise complex ideas with specific goals", "fol": "Slide 2", "vs": "natural language", "n": "natfor"}, {"t": "syntax", "zh": "句法", "b": "comp", "d": "The rules for constructing sentences.", "zd": "怎样构造句子的规则.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "Have syntax (rules for constructing sentences) and semantics (meaning conveyed by words and sentences)", "fol": "Slide 3", "vs": "semantics", "n": "natfor", "ns": "natfor.synsem"}, {"t": "semantics", "zh": "语义", "b": "comp", "d": "The meaning conveyed by words and sentences.", "zd": "词和句子表达的意义.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "Have syntax (rules for constructing sentences) and semantics (meaning conveyed by words and sentences)", "fol": "Slide 3", "vs": "syntax", "n": "natfor", "ns": "natfor.synsem"}, {"t": "grammar", "zh": "文法", "b": "comp", "d": "The set of production rules of a language.", "zd": "一门语言的产生式规则.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "sprache", "alt": ["production rules"], "n": "natfor", "ns": "natfor.struct"}, {"t": "interoperability", "zh": "互操作性", "b": "comp", "d": "The ability of formal languages to work on different systems and devices.", "zd": "在不同系统和设备上都能用.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "staerken", "q": "Interoperability → work on different systems and devices (e.g., HTML)", "fol": "Slide 5", "n": "flsw", "ns": "flsw.interop"}, {"t": "domain specificity", "zh": "领域专用", "b": "comp", "d": "Formal languages work well, but mostly only within a specific domain.", "zd": "效果好, 但多半只在特定领域有效.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "staerken", "q": "Domain specificity → work well but mostly for specific domains (e.g., logic, close classes)", "fol": "Slide 6", "n": "flsw", "ns": "flsw.domain"}, {"t": "determinism", "zh": "确定性", "b": "comp", "d": "The same input always yields the same output.", "zd": "同样的输入总得到同样的输出.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "staerken", "q": "Precision and predictability → control and determinism", "fol": "Slide 5", "n": "flsw", "ns": "flsw.precise"}, {"t": "membership", "zh": "成员关系", "b": "comp", "d": "Whether a given string belongs to a set of strings.", "zd": "一个串是否属于某个串集合.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "berechnung", "q": "Determining the membership in a set of strings", "fol": "Slide 8", "vs": "transduction", "n": "member"}, {"t": "transduction", "zh": "转换", "b": "comp", "d": "Mapping input strings of one language to output strings of another.", "zd": "把输入串转换成输出串.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "warum", "vs": "membership", "n": "member"}, {"t": "primitive", "zh": "基本元素", "b": "comp", "d": "The basic elements that rules combine into complex structures in a computation.", "zd": "计算中被规则组合成复杂结构的基本单位.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "berechnung", "q": "Computers are built on those basic primitives (0/1) and operations over them (and/or/not/xor/. . . )", "fol": "Slide 9", "alt": ["primitives"], "n": "compu", "ns": "compu.prim"}, {"t": "replicability", "zh": "可重复性", "b": "comp", "d": "A computation must always give the same output for the same input.", "zd": "同样的输入必须总得到同样的输出.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "berechnung", "q": "Replicability: it should always provide the same output given the same input", "fol": "Slide 9", "n": "compu", "ns": "compu.repli"}, {"t": "Turing machine", "zh": "图灵机", "b": "comp", "d": "A theoretical model of a general purpose computer.", "zd": "通用计算机的理论模型.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "turing", "q": "The Turing machine: a theoretical model of a general purpose computer", "fol": "Slide 10", "n": "turing"}, {"t": "Turing test", "zh": "图灵测试", "b": "comp", "d": "A test whether a human judge can tell a machine from a human in a conversation.", "zd": "评判者在对话中能否分辨机器和人.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "turing", "q": "The Turing test: is a machine really intelligent? → can a human judge discriminate between a human participant and a machine by talking to them in natural language", "fol": "Slide 10", "n": "turing", "ns": "turing.ttest"}, {"t": "Chomsky hierarchy", "zh": "乔姆斯基谱系", "b": "comp", "d": "A classification of formal languages into four levels by the power of their grammars.", "zd": "按文法的能力把形式语言分成四级.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "geschichte", "n": "clhist", "ns": "clhist.chomsky"}, {"t": "context-free grammar", "zh": "上下文无关文法", "b": "comp", "d": "The formalism used today for syntactic structures in computational linguistics.", "zd": "今天计算语言学里描述句法结构的形式工具.", "f": "FS-01-导论.html", "a": "heute", "q": "syntactic structures → Context-free grammars", "fol": "Slide 14", "alt": ["CFG"], "n": "hybrid", "ns": "hybrid.apps"}, {"t": "alphabet", "zh": "字母表", "b": "str", "d": "A finite and non-empty set of symbols.", "zd": "有限且非空的符号集合.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "def-alphabet", "q": "An alphabet is a finite and non-empty set of symbols", "fol": "Slide 2", "n": "alpha"}, {"t": "string", "zh": "字符串", "b": "str", "d": "Any ordered and finite sequence of symbols from an alphabet.", "zd": "由字母表中符号组成的有序且有限的序列.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "def-string", "q": "Strings are the basic elements of a language", "fol": "Slide 3", "vs": "language", "alt": ["word"], "n": "string"}, {"t": "empty string", "zh": "空串", "b": "str", "d": "The sequence with no symbols, written ε.", "zd": "不含任何符号的串, 记作 ε.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "def-string", "vs": "empty set", "alt": ["null string"], "n": "string", "ns": "string.eps"}, {"t": "universal language", "zh": "全语言", "b": "str", "d": "The set of all strings over a given alphabet, written Σ*.", "zd": "给定字母表上所有串的集合 Σ*.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "universal", "q": "Universal language: The set of all strings over a given alphabet", "fol": "Slide 5", "vs": "positive closure", "n": "univ"}, {"t": "positive closure", "zh": "正闭包", "b": "str", "d": "The set of all strings over an alphabet except the empty string, written Σ⁺.", "zd": "除空串以外所有串的集合 Σ⁺.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "plus", "vs": "universal language", "n": "plus"}, {"t": "Kleene star", "zh": "Kleene 星号", "b": "str", "d": "The star in Σ*, meaning zero or more repetitions.", "zd": "Σ* 里的星号, 表示零次或多次.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "universal", "n": "univ", "ns": "univ.kleene"}, {"t": "concatenation", "zh": "连接", "b": "sops", "d": "The string obtained by appending the symbols of the second string after the first.", "zd": "把第二个串接在第一个串后面得到的串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "konkat", "n": "konkat"}, {"t": "length", "zh": "长度", "b": "sops", "d": "The number of symbols in a string, written |w|.", "zd": "串中符号的个数 |w|.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "laenge", "q": "Static (cannot be modified) and with finite length", "fol": "Slide 6", "n": "len"}, {"t": "index", "zh": "下标", "b": "sops", "d": "The symbol at the i-th position of a string, counted from the left.", "zd": "从左数第 i 个位置上的符号.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "index", "n": "index"}, {"t": "symbol occurrence number", "zh": "符号出现次数", "b": "sops", "d": "The number of occurrences of a symbol in a string, written |w|ₜ.", "zd": "某个符号在串中出现的次数.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "vorkommen", "n": "occ"}, {"t": "reverse", "zh": "反转", "b": "sops", "d": "The string obtained by writing the symbols in reverse order, written wᴿ.", "zd": "把串的符号倒过来写.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "reverse", "n": "rev"}, {"t": "palindrome", "zh": "回文", "b": "sops", "d": "A string that equals its own reverse.", "zd": "反转后和自己相同的串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "reverse", "n": "rev", "ns": "rev.palin"}, {"t": "exponentiation", "zh": "幂", "b": "sops", "d": "Concatenating a string with itself n times, written wⁿ.", "zd": "把串和自己连接 n 次.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "power", "vs": "power", "n": "pow"}, {"t": "language", "zh": "语言", "b": "lops", "d": "Any subset of the universal language, i.e. any set of strings over an alphabet.", "zd": "全语言的任意子集, 也就是任意一个串集合.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "If the language has a finite number of sentences, this is a finite language", "fol": "Slide 15", "vs": "string", "n": "lang"}, {"t": "sentence", "zh": "句子", "b": "lops", "d": "A string that belongs to a language.", "zd": "属于某个语言的串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "If the language has a finite number of sentences, this is a finite language", "fol": "Slide 15", "n": "lang", "ns": "lang.sent"}, {"t": "finite language", "zh": "有限语言", "b": "lops", "d": "A language with a finite number of sentences.", "zd": "句子个数有限的语言.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "sprache", "q": "If the language has a finite number of sentences, this is a finite language", "fol": "Slide 15", "vs": "infinite language", "n": "lang", "ns": "lang.fininf"}, {"t": "infinite language", "zh": "无限语言", "b": "lops", "d": "A language with infinitely many sentences.", "zd": "句子个数无限的语言.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "sprache", "vs": "finite language", "n": "lang", "ns": "lang.fininf"}, {"t": "union", "zh": "并", "b": "lops", "d": "The set of strings valid in at least one of two languages.", "zd": "至少属于其中一个语言的串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "union", "q": "Union: the set of strings valid in at least one of the languages", "fol": "Slide 16", "vs": "intersection", "n": "setops"}, {"t": "intersection", "zh": "交", "b": "lops", "d": "The set of strings valid in both languages.", "zd": "同时属于两个语言的串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "union", "q": "Intersection: the set of strings valid for both languages", "fol": "Slide 16", "vs": "union", "n": "setops"}, {"t": "complement", "zh": "补", "b": "lops", "d": "All strings of Σ* that are not in the language.", "zd": "Σ* 中不属于该语言的所有串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "komplement", "vs": "difference", "n": "compl"}, {"t": "difference", "zh": "差", "b": "lops", "d": "The strings that are in L₁ but not in L₂.", "zd": "属于 L₁ 但不属于 L₂ 的串.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "komplement", "vs": "complement", "n": "compl"}, {"t": "power", "zh": "幂", "b": "lops", "d": "A language concatenated with itself n times, with L⁰ = {ε}.", "zd": "语言和自己连接 n 次, 规定 L⁰ = {ε}.", "f": "FS-02-字母表字符串与语言.html", "a": "potenz", "q": "Powers of a L: concatenation for a certain number of times", "fol": "Slide 18", "vs": "exponentiation", "n": "lpow"}, {"t": "finite state automaton", "zh": "有限状态自动机", "b": "fsa", "d": "A machine that reads an input string symbol by symbol and changes between a finite set of states.", "zd": "逐个读输入符号、在有限个状态之间转换的机器.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "graph", "q": "Can all be implemented as finite state automata", "fol": "Slide 3", "alt": ["FSA", "finite automaton"], "n": "fsm"}, {"t": "state", "zh": "状态", "b": "fsa", "d": "A situation in which the system remains an amount of time.", "zd": "系统停留一段时间的情形.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "graph", "q": "State: situation in which the system remains an amount of time", "fol": "Slide 4", "vs": "transition", "n": "fsm", "ns": "fsm.fsmstate"}, {"t": "transition", "zh": "转移", "b": "fsa", "d": "An action that happens instantly and moves the automaton from one state to another.", "zd": "瞬间发生、让自动机换状态的动作.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "graph", "q": "Event/transition: action that happens instantly", "fol": "Slide 4", "vs": "state", "n": "fsm", "ns": "fsm.fsmtrans"}, {"t": "directed graph", "zh": "有向图", "b": "fsa", "d": "A finite set of nodes (states) connected by a set of directed arcs (transitions).", "zd": "由有向边 (转移) 连起来的有限个节点 (状态).", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "graph", "q": "Represented as a directed graph: a finite set of nodes (states) connected by a set of directed arcs (transitions)", "fol": "Slide 4"}, {"t": "input tape", "zh": "输入带", "b": "fsa", "d": "Contains the input string to be processed; static, finite and read from left to right.", "zd": "存放输入串, 不能改写、长度有限、从左到右读.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "q": "Contains the input string to be processed", "fol": "Slide 6", "n": "tape"}, {"t": "reader head", "zh": "读头", "b": "fsa", "d": "Reads one symbol at a time from the input tape and moves one step to the right.", "zd": "一次读一个符号再右移一格.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "q": "Reads a symbol and then moves one step to the right", "fol": "Slide 7", "n": "head"}, {"t": "control unit", "zh": "控制单元", "b": "fsa", "d": "Determines transitions between states; consists of the state register and the transition function.", "zd": "决定状态转移, 由状态寄存器和转移函数组成.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "q": "Determines transitions between states", "fol": "Slide 8", "n": "cunit"}, {"t": "state register", "zh": "状态寄存器", "b": "fsa", "d": "The part of the control unit that tracks the current state.", "zd": "控制单元里记住当前状态的部分.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "teile", "q": "State Register: Tracks the current state", "fol": "Slide 8", "n": "cunit", "ns": "cunit.register"}, {"t": "start state", "zh": "初始状态", "b": "fdef", "d": "The state the control unit is set to before reading the input, written q₀.", "zd": "读输入之前控制单元所处的状态 q₀.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "ablauf", "q": "Control unit set to the start state", "fol": "Slide 9", "vs": "accept state", "alt": ["initial state"], "n": "quint", "ns": "quint.qinit"}, {"t": "accept state", "zh": "接受状态", "b": "fdef", "d": "A state in F; the input is accepted if the automaton is in such a state after reading it.", "zd": "终态集合 F 里的状态, 读完输入时在这里就接受.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "ablauf", "q": "Accepts if in an accept/final state", "fol": "Slide 9", "vs": "start state", "alt": ["final state"]}, {"t": "deterministic FSA", "zh": "确定性有限自动机", "b": "fsa", "d": "An FSA with exactly one transition for every state and input symbol.", "zd": "每个状态和输入符号恰好一个转移的 FSA.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "det", "q": "For every state and input symbol, there is exactly one transition to a new state", "fol": "Slide 11", "vs": "nondeterministic FSA", "alt": ["DFA"], "n": "dfa"}, {"t": "nondeterministic FSA", "zh": "非确定性有限自动机", "b": "fsa", "d": "An FSA that may have multiple possible transitions for a given state and input symbol.", "zd": "同一状态和输入符号可以有多个转移的 FSA.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "det", "q": "It may have multiple possible transitions for a given state and input symbol", "fol": "Slide 11", "vs": "deterministic FSA", "alt": ["NFA"], "n": "nfa"}, {"t": "quintuple", "zh": "五元组", "b": "fdef", "d": "The formal definition of an FSA as (Σ, Q, q₀, δ, F).", "zd": "把 FSA 写成 (Σ, Q, q₀, δ, F).", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "quintupel", "q": "FSA is a Quintuple", "fol": "Slide 13", "n": "quint"}, {"t": "transition function", "zh": "转移函数", "b": "fdef", "d": "δ : Q × Σ → Q, defines how the state changes in response to an input symbol.", "zd": "δ : Q × Σ → Q, 规定状态怎样随输入符号变化.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "delta", "q": "It defines how the state of the automaton changes in response to an input symbol", "fol": "Slide 14", "vs": "transition table", "n": "delta"}, {"t": "transition table", "zh": "转移表", "b": "fdef", "d": "A table with states as rows and input symbols as columns giving the next state.", "zd": "行是状态、列是输入符号、格子是下一个状态的表.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "delta", "vs": "transition function", "n": "ttable"}, {"t": "complete FSA", "zh": "完全的 FSA", "b": "cmpl", "d": "An FSA with transitions defined for all input symbols in every state.", "zd": "每个状态对所有输入符号都有转移的 FSA.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "complete", "q": "It has transitions defined for all input symbols", "fol": "Slide 18", "vs": "incomplete FSA", "n": "complete"}, {"t": "incomplete FSA", "zh": "不完全的 FSA", "b": "cmpl", "d": "An FSA with missing transitions for certain inputs in some states.", "zd": "有些状态对某些输入缺转移的 FSA.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "unvollst", "q": "This automaton has missing transitions for certain inputs in some states", "fol": "Slide 22", "vs": "complete FSA", "n": "incompl"}, {"t": "sink state", "zh": "陷阱状态", "b": "cmpl", "d": "A non-accepting state that the FSA never leaves once entered.", "zd": "进入后就出不来的非接受状态.", "f": "FS-03-有限状态自动机.html", "a": "sink", "q": "Once entered, the FSA remains in this state", "fol": "Slide 20", "alt": ["dead state", "trap state"], "n": "sink"}], "newf": []});